.TH KEMPT 1 "2026-10-03" "Kempt" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kempt \- tidy dnf and Flatpak updates for Fedora, from the terminal or the Plasma panel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kempt
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.PP
.B kempt check
.RB [ \-\-refresh ]
.RB [ \-\-anyway ]
.RB [ \-\-coalesce ]
.RB [ \-\-strict ]
.br
.B kempt update
.RB [ \-\-no\-flatpak ]
.RB [ \-\-surface=\c
.IR surface ]
.RB [ \-\-risky\-ok ]
.br
.B kempt run
.RB [ \-\-print\-command ]
.RB [ \-\-surface=\c
.IR surface ]
.RB [ \-\-risky\-ok ]
.br
.B kempt unstage
.br
.B kempt reclaim
.RB [ \-\-list ]
.RB [ \-y ]
.RB [ \-\-expect=\fIdigest\fR ]
.br
.B kempt summary
.RI [ N ]
.br
.B kempt summary \-\-json
.br
.B kempt history
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B kempt log
.RB [ \-n
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-raw ]
.br
.B kempt doctor
.br
.B kempt hold
.IR backend : name
.br
.B kempt unhold
.IR backend : name
.br
.B kempt holds
.RB [ \-\-exclude\-args ]
.br
.B kempt config get
.I key
.RI [ default ]
.br
.B kempt config set
.I key value
.br
.B kempt enable\-passwordless
.br
.B kempt disable\-passwordless
.br
.B kempt discover\-notifier
.BR off " | " on " | " keep " | " status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B kempt help
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B kempt \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kempt
finds and installs pending system updates from dnf5 and Flatpak. It is also the engine behind the
Kempt Plasma panel widget, which runs these same commands. The widget is described in
.IR docs/widget.md .
.PP
A held package is left out of every Kempt run, and still shows as pending. When an update touches
packages your running session depends on, such as the kernel, systemd, Qt or KDE, Kempt recommends
installing it on the next restart.
.PP
Only two small helpers run as root, one per polkit action, and both check every argument. Both
serve dnf. Flatpak updates run as you and never ask for a password.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR check " [" \-\-refresh "] [" \-\-anyway "] [" \-\-coalesce "] [" \-\-strict ]
Ask every enabled backend what is pending, write the state file and print it as JSON. A check
answers from the local dnf and Flatpak caches. It refreshes them at most once every three hours,
and never on battery or a metered connection.
.B \-\-refresh
fetches now, but still skips battery and metered connections.
.B \-\-anyway
fetches now even on battery or a metered connection, for this check only.
.B \-\-coalesce
is for automatic checks: when this check waited for another that succeeded later, that one's state
is printed and nothing is queried.
.B \-\-refresh
turns it off.
.B \-\-strict
exits 1 when the answer is not current: a backend failed, the per\-user Flatpak apps could not be
listed, or another check held the lock and the previous state was printed.
.IP
When a backend fails, its
.B status
is
.BR stale ,
the error is recorded and the previous items are kept. Without
.BR \-\-strict ,
that still exits 0.
.B "Empty output with exit 0 means no data, never zero updates."
A check also records a staged update once the restart has installed it.
.TP
.BR update " [" \-\-no\-flatpak "] [" \-\-surface= \c
.IR surface "] [" \c
.BR \-\-risky\-ok ]
Run the update now, in this process. Options override the configuration file for this run.
.B \-\-no\-flatpak
updates system packages only.
.B \-\-surface=
picks where the run happens:
.BR terminal ", " widget ", " background " or " offline .
An unknown value logs a warning and uses
.BR terminal .
Held items are skipped, and the summary lists them.
.IP
When session\-critical packages are pending, a terminal run asks first: stage for the next
restart, update now, or abort. Enter, Ctrl\-D or a second unknown answer aborts, with exit 0 and
nothing changed. A run that cannot ask sends a notification and carries on.
.B \-\-risky\-ok
leaves that notification out. The widget passes it after
.BR "Install Now" .
.IP
.B \-\-surface=offline
downloads the update and sets it to install on the next restart, with one password prompt. Any
restart then installs it. Kempt never restarts the machine itself. If the update cannot be set up
for the restart, the run fails and Kempt discards it. A later live update that changes any system
package discards the stage.
.IP
When another program holds the dnf or Flatpak lock, Kempt tries three times, 10 seconds apart.
Exit 5: an image\-based Fedora (Silverblue, Kinoite, Bazzite or a bootc image), installed packages or
apps that could not be read, or
.B \-\-surface=offline
while a Fedora release upgrade is stored, because staging would cancel it. Exit 7: the only
failure was that lock, held through all three tries. A busy lock while rebuilding a staged update
exits 1.
.TP
.BR run " [" \-\-print\-command "] [" \-\-surface= \c
.IR surface "] [" \c
.BR \-\-risky\-ok ]
Start
.B kempt update
where the
.B surface
setting says, then return at once. The widget's
.B Update Now
runs this.
.B \-\-print\-command
prints the launch command and starts nothing.
.B \-\-risky\-ok
is passed on to an update outside the terminal. A terminal run still asks.
Exit 0 means the update started. The state file and
.B kempt history
have the result. Exit 5: the terminal window did not open within five seconds.
.TP
.B unstage
Discard the update staged for the next restart. It asks for your password once, unless nothing is
staged. Kempt keeps its record until dnf5 confirms the transaction is gone. Exit 1: the root helper
failed, or dnf5 still has the transaction. Exit 3: another update is running. Exit 5: a Fedora
release upgrade is stored, another updater has prepared the next restart, or the root helper
refused.
.TP
.BR reclaim " [" \-\-list "] [" \-y "] [" \-\-expect= \c
.IR digest ]
Remove the system Flatpak runtimes no installed app uses, after showing them and their estimated
size.
.B \-\-list
only shows them.
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
removes without asking.
.BI \-\-expect= digest
removes only if the list still matches
.B reclaim.digest
from the state file.
.IP
A runtime is removed only after it has been unused for an hour, counted from the first check that
listed it. Runtimes go first, then the extensions still unused, so an app installed meanwhile keeps
its own. A pinned runtime is never removed: use
.B "flatpak pin"
to keep one.
.IP
It never asks for a password. Removing needs an administrator logged in at the desktop, and it
refuses to run as root. Exit 5: nothing removed, because it ran as root, Flatpak is off or missing,
.B reclaim=off
is set, removing needs an administrator, or there is no
.B \-y
and no terminal to ask at. Exit 6: the list is not the set you were shown, or part of it became
unused less than an hour ago. Exit 1: Flatpak failed, possibly after removing some. Run
.B "kempt reclaim \-\-list"
to see what is left.
.TP
.BR summary " [" \c
.IR N ]
Show one run as text.
.I N
counts back from the newest and defaults to 1. A damaged entry is skipped with a warning.
.TP
.B summary \-\-json
Print the newest run's history entry as JSON, for the widget. It takes no
.IR N .
With no runs, or a damaged newest entry, it prints nothing and shows no older run instead.
.TP
.BR history " [" \-\-json ]
List past runs, newest first: time, how it ran, status and what changed.
.B \-\-json
prints them as one JSON array of
.B "summary \-\-json"
entries, or
.BR [] .
A damaged entry is left out and named on stderr.
.TP
.BR log " [" \-n " " \c
.IR N "] [" \c
.BR \-\-raw ]
Print the event log, newest last, as sentences.
.I N
defaults to 30.
.B \-\-raw
prints the lines as
.I events.log
stores them. Each line is
.IR "timestamp via text" ,
where
.I via
is
.B widget
or
.BR cli .
It answers "did the change I just made land?", which the run logs and history cannot.
.TP
.B doctor
Check this install and print one line per check, marked
.BR ok ", " info ", " WARN " or " FAIL .
It covers the root helpers and the polkit action, the tools Kempt needs, the configuration file,
the state directory and any staged update. Every check runs, and the last five events follow.
Exit 1 when any line is
.BR FAIL .
A staged update that was downloaded but never set to install is a
.BR FAIL ,
and
.B "sudo dnf5 offline clean"
removes it.
.IP
Run it when the widget says it cannot check, or shows counts you do not trust. A missing root
helper makes every dnf check fail, so the system package count never changes.
.IP
The report ends with the install. In a checkout,
.BR helpers: ", " policy: " and " widget:
compare the installed copies with the checkout.
.B DIFFER
means you pulled without re\-running
.BR ./install.sh ,
and the line names the fix. A packaged install prints
.B "install: packaged"
instead.
.TP
.BI hold " backend:name"
Skip a package or app in Kempt runs, and keep reporting it as pending.
.I backend
is
.B dnf
or
.BR flatpak .
Flatpak runtimes cannot be held. Holds are Kempt's own list, which a
.B dnf5
command of your own ignores.
.TP
.BI unhold " backend:name"
Remove a hold. Removing one that is not there succeeds.
.TP
.BR holds " [" \-\-exclude\-args ]
List current holds, one
.I backend:name
per line.
.B \-\-exclude\-args
prints the dnf holds as one line of dnf5
.B \-\-exclude=
arguments, or an empty line with none, for
.BR "sudo dnf5 upgrade $(kempt holds \-\-exclude\-args)" .
.TP
.BI "config get" " key " [ default ]
Print a setting. With no value stored, it prints
.IR default ,
or the built\-in default for a known key.
.TP
.BI "config set" " key value"
Change a setting. Keys match
.RB ' ^[a-z][a-z0-9_]+$ '
and values are one line. An unknown key, or a value the key does not accept, gets a warning on
stderr and is stored anyway, so a newer widget can use it.
.B "config set surface widget"
stores
.BR popup ,
the value the widget reads.
.TP
.B enable\-passwordless
Install a polkit rule that lets your active local session install dnf updates without a password.
It asks for your password once.
.TP
.B disable\-passwordless
Remove that rule. Removing a rule that was never installed succeeds.
.TP
.BR "discover\-notifier off" " | " on " | " keep " | " status " [" \-\-json ]
Turn Discover's own update notifier off or back on for you alone, without a password.
.B off
writes
.I ~/.config/autostart/org.kde.discover.notifier.desktop
with
.B Hidden=true
and stops the running notifier. A file of your own there moves to a name ending in
.IR .before\-kempt .
.B on
removes Kempt's file, puts yours back and starts the notifier. An edited Kempt file moves to a
name ending in
.IR .kempt\-edited .
.B keep
changes nothing and records that you answered the widget's offer.
.B status
says whether the notifier is installed, on, turned off by Kempt and running.
.B \-\-json
prints the same as one object.
.IP
Exit 1, with nothing changed:
.B off
found a
.I .before\-kempt
copy already there,
.B on
found a file of your own keeping the notifier off, or the path is a directory or a broken
symlink.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " version ", " \-V
Print
.RB ' "kempt <version>" '
from the
.I VERSION
file, or
.RB ' "kempt unknown" '
without one.
.TP
.BR help " [" \c
.IR command "], " \c
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print the command list. A bare
.B kempt
prints it too, and an unknown command prints it on stderr and exits 2.
.BI "help " command
prints that command's usage, and so does
.B \-\-help
or
.B \-h
right after a command.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings live in
.I ~/.config/kempt/config
as
.IR key = value
lines. Read and change them with
.BR "kempt config" ,
or in the widget's settings. The keys are
.BR include_flatpak " (default " true "),"
.BR auto_accept " (default " true "),"
.BR surface " (default " popup "),"
.BR refresh_interval_min " (default " 60 "),"
.BR widget_icon_size " (default " auto "),"
.BR restart_reminder " (default " true "),"
.BR risky_regex " and"
.BR reclaim " (" ask ", " automatic " or " off "; default " ask ")."
A boolean is true when it is
.BR true ", " 1 " or " yes .
Everything else is false.
.PP
The full reference is
.IR docs/configuration.md .
.SH FILES
Where two paths are given, the first is the package and the second a checkout install. Files in
your home directory are the same for both.
.TP
.IR /usr/bin/kempt " or " ~/.local/bin/kempt
The command, a symlink into
.I /usr/share/kempt
or the checkout.
.TP
.IR /usr/share/kempt/VERSION " or " <checkout>/VERSION
The version that
.B kempt \-\-version
prints.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kempt/config
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kempt/holds
Holds, one
.I backend:name
per line.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kempt/state.json
The latest check result, schema v1. Scripts and the widget read it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kempt/history/
One JSON entry per run. The newest 50 are kept.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kempt/logs/
The raw output of each run, deleted after 60 days.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kempt/events.log
The event log, mode 0600. Past 2500 lines it is cut to the last 2000.
.TP
.IR /usr/libexec/kempt-refresh " or " /usr/local/libexec/kempt-refresh
Root helper: refreshes package metadata, with no password prompt.
.TP
.IR /usr/libexec/kempt-apply " or " /usr/local/libexec/kempt-apply
Root helper: runs the dnf upgrade, with one password prompt per run.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.erez_c137.kempt.policy
The two polkit actions. Each names one helper path, and
.B kempt doctor
fails when it is not the one this CLI uses.
.TP
.I /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/49-kempt.rules
Present only while passwordless mode is on.
.TP
.IR /usr/share/plasma/plasmoids/io.github.erez_c137.kempt/ " or " ~/.local/share/plasma/plasmoids/io.github.erez_c137.kempt/
The Plasma widget. A checkout install copies it, so re\-run
.B ./install.sh
after changing
.IR plasmoid/ .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Most commands use these codes. Each command above lists its own cases.
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Something failed. This includes a busy writers' lock:
.BR "config set" ,
.BR hold ,
.B unhold
and
.B "discover\-notifier off|on|keep"
give up after 30 seconds and write nothing.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command, option or argument.
.TP
.B 3
Cannot start:
.B jq
is missing, or another
.B kempt update
is running.
.TP
.B 4
No terminal emulator.
.TP
.B 5
Stopped before changing anything.
.TP
.B 6
.B reclaim
only: the list changed. Nothing was removed.
.TP
.B 7
.B update
only: another program held the package lock.
.TP
.B 8
Run as root. Run Kempt as your own user, and it asks for a password when it needs one.
.PP
.B disable\-passwordless
passes on
.BR pkexec 's
code when it cannot remove the rule: 126 when the password dialog was dismissed, 127 when
authorization was refused.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnf5 (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR polkit (8)
.PP
The package installs the full documentation in
.IR /usr/share/doc/kempt/ :
.IR docs/usage.md " for every command, " docs/widget.md " for the widget, and"
.IR docs/configuration.md ", " docs/architecture.md " and " docs/security.md .
A checkout has the same files, and they are also at https://github.com/erez-c137/kempt.
